<description>&lt;p&gt;The junta is destroying bridges in Arakan and planning a 108‑kilometre fence along the Bangladesh border while continuing airstrikes, including a strike that killed 12 people at a displacement camp in Rakhine state and a double-tap attack on civilians. ASEAN leaders have extended the ban on Myanmar’s junta leaders, pledged calibrated engagement and tied any return to summit participation to measurable progress on the peace plan. The military is also advancing west of the Sittaung River, prompting further civilian flight. The conflict caused 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/15/myanmar-rohingya-genocide-icj&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-until-there-is-meaningful-progress-on-its-peace-plan/a-79951878?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-rdf&quot;&gt;Deutsche Welle&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261116-verdict-week-in-the-myanmar-genocide-case&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Straits Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiVkFVX3lxTE9HbjNHSGliMkdBU2RZbWk0M3JtazNyNWR5ZTJZRnZuMUdNSDNtREFvcVJyY1pPekhvMkd0QnI2RUIxMkxOc0daeFpOVHhKMF9CZnB6TE93?oc=5&quot;&gt;Shan Herald Agency for News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi_?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Times of India&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxPSEh3WFBsLUFzeE1yQzh4N21iY3I3RVJjcHFpWm9OXzV0UjFIWW41RVZUQXh6dGUzc